Hi Dad,

Here is everything you need to get your retirement statements from LACERA =
as PDF files you can save or print. I broke it into small steps. You do no=
t need to do it all at once.

Quick background: LACERA is the Los Angeles County Employees Retirement As=
sociation. It is the pension system that pays your Sheriff's Department re=
tirement. Because you were with the Sheriff's Department, you are what the=
y call a "Safety" member. Their website has a section for retirees where y=
ou can download all your statements yourself, any time, day or night.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
THE TWO THINGS TO WRITE DOWN
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

PHONE NUMBER (LACERA Member Services):   800-786-6464
     Monday through Friday, 7:00 a.m. to 5:30 p.m. Pacific time

WEBSITE TO LOG IN:   https://home.mylacera.gov

Those are the only two things you really need. Everything below is just de=
tail.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
STEP 1 - CALL THEM FIRST AND GET AN ACCOUNT SET UP
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

Since you don't have an online account yet, the easiest path by far is to =
call them and let a person walk you through it. Do this step first.

Call:  800-786-6464
When:  Monday through Friday, 7:00 a.m. to 5:30 p.m. Pacific

Tell them: "I'm a retired member and I'd like to set up my online My LACER=
A account so I can download my statements."

Have this in front of you before you dial:
  * Your full legal name as it appears on your pension
  * Your Social Security number
  * Your date of birth
  * Your current mailing address (the one LACERA has on file for you)
  * An email address you can check - the website logs you in with an email=
 address and a password, not a member number
  * A pen and paper to write down your new password

Two questions to ask them while you have them on the phone:
  1. "Can I finish the sign-up right now online, or do you have to mail me=
 a registration code first?" (Some systems mail you a code. If they do, ju=
st watch the mail for it and then do Step 2.)
  2. "Can you turn on paperless delivery for my account?" (This makes all =
your future statements show up in the website automatically. Worth saying =
yes to.)

If you get stuck at any point, that same number - 800-786-6464 - is the ri=
ght number to call back. You will not be bothering them. This is exactly w=
hat that line is for.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
STEP 2 - LOG IN TO THE WEBSITE
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

Open your web browser and go to:

    https://home.mylacera.gov

The full address, if you want to type it exactly, is:
    https://home.mylacera.gov/lmpublic/login.xhtml

Sign in with the email address and password you set up in Step 1.

If you forget your password, there is a "forgot my password" link right on=
 that page. Click it and it will email you a reset link.

The site is called "My LACERA." It is open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
STEP 3 - DOWNLOAD YOUR STATEMENTS
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

Once you are logged in, look for the documents or statements area. These a=
re the things you can download as PDF files:

  * ANNUAL BENEFIT STATEMENT - your yearly summary. Shows your service cre=
dit, your contributions, and who you have named as beneficiaries. LACERA i=
ssues it the month after your birthday.

  * 1099-R TAX FORMS - your pension tax form, one for each tax year. This =
is the one the tax preparer asks for.

  * AUTOMATIC DEPOSIT RECEIPTS (they call them "ADRs") - these are your mo=
nthly paystubs. Shows the deposit amount and any withholdings and deductio=
ns.

  * PENSION VERIFICATION LETTER - a proof-of-income letter. This is the on=
e to grab if a landlord, a lender, or a senior housing application ever as=
ks you to prove your monthly income.

Each one will have a download or print button. Click it and the PDF saves =
to your computer, usually into your "Downloads" folder.

While you are in there, you can also update your address, change your tax =
withholding, change your direct deposit bank, or update your beneficiaries=
=2E You do not have to call for any of that once you have the login.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
STEP 4 - SEND ME COPIES
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

Once you have them downloaded, email me the PDFs and I'll keep an organize=
d copy on my end so we always have a backup:

  * Your most recent Annual Benefit Statement
  * Your latest 1099-R
  * A few of the recent monthly deposit receipts

One note: these files have your Social Security number and account details=
 on them. Don't post them anywhere or send them to anyone who asks out of =
the blue. If someone calls you claiming to be from LACERA and asks for you=
r information, hang up and call 800-786-6464 yourself.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D
ALL THE LACERA CONTACT INFORMATION, IN ONE PLACE
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

PHONE
  Member Services (start here)  800-786-6464   Mon-Fri, 7:00 a.m.-5:30 p.m=
=2E PT
  Retiree Healthcare            800-786-6464   Mon-Fri, 7:00 a.m.-5:30 p.m=
=2E PT
  Main business line            626-564-6000   Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m.-5:00 p.m=
=2E PT
  From outside the U.S.         626-564-6132   Mon-Fri, 7:00 a.m.-5:30 p.m=
=2E PT
  Fax                           626-564-6155

EMAIL
  General retirement questions   welcome@lacera.gov
  Retiree healthcare             healthcare@lacera.gov

IN PERSON (appointment required - they do not take walk-ins)
  LACERA Member Service Center
  300 N. Lake Avenue, Suite 100
  Pasadena, CA 91101
  Mon-Fri, 7:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m., closed for lunch 12:00-1:00 p.m.
  Closed on County holidays

MAIL
  LACERA
  P.O. Box 7060
  Pasadena, CA 91109-7060

WEBSITES
  Log in here                    https://home.mylacera.gov
  Main LACERA website            https://www.lacera.gov
  About the online account       https://www.lacera.gov/my-lacera
  Setup help videos              https://www.lacera.gov/getting-started-my=
-lacera
  Retirees section               https://www.lacera.gov/retirees-and-famil=
ies
  Retirement payments info       https://www.lacera.gov/retirement-payment=
s

One small warning: the real site is lacera.GOV, not .com. Stick with .gov.

=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

If any of this gets frustrating, just call me and we'll do it together on =
the phone, or I'll come over and we'll sit down and knock it out in twenty=
 minutes. Honestly, Step 1 is the only hard part. After that it's just log=
ging in.

Love you, Dad.

Bryan

